{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107146","id":2570033743,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6ZL5pP","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107146","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107146.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107146.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107146","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107146/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107146/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107146/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/7515c0c37dca0067f2e8c51d2f7d3132eb679ef1","number":107146,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[.NET] Add web export support for C# projects in Godot 4","user":{"login":"Enrique726","id":186024179,"node_id":"U_kgDOCxaA8w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186024179?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726","html_url":"https://github.com/Enrique726","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Enrique726/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR adds web platform export support for C# (.NET) projects in Godot 4, a feature that was available in Godot 3.x but was removed in Godot 4 due to changes in the .NET runtime architecture (moving from Mono to CoreCLR).\r\n\r\n## Implementation\r\nThis implementation is based on the approach used in PR #106125, leveraging static linking of Mono for WebAssembly exports. The key components are:\r\n\r\n1. **Web Platform Recognition**\r\n   - Added web platform to the list of supported platforms in ExportPlugin.cs\r\n   - Added special condition in config.py to allow mono module on web platform\r\n\r\n2. **WebAssembly Integration**\r\n   - Added \"wasm\" architecture support in runtime identifier mapping\r\n   - Added web-specific path handling in godotsharp_dirs.cpp\r\n\r\n3. **Mono Runtime Integration**\r\n   - Implemented static linking and initialization of Mono for WebAssembly in gd_mono.cpp\r\n   - Added web platform specific initialization sequence\r\n\r\n4. **Build System Support**\r\n   - Created web_export_template.py for building WebAssembly-compatible export templates\r\n\r\n## Known Limitations\r\n- Exported games have large file sizes (~70+ MiB) due to the embedded Mono runtime\r\n- Compression should be used to reduce file size (~24 MiB with compression)\r\n- Some .NET APIs may not function correctly in browser environments due to WebAssembly/browser limitations\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\nThis implementation has been tested with basic C# projects exported to web platform, verifying that:\r\n- C# code executes correctly in browser environment\r\n- Basic Godot API access works as expected\r\n- Project builds and exports successfully\r\n\r\n## References\r\n- Related issue: #70796 (Document missing C# web export templates due to lack of upstream support)","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"no